{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>He commanded them</b> — Three times in the Masorah: ויעשו בניו לו כן כאשר צום · ואידך הוקם את דברי יונדב אשר צום · פן תאמרו עצבי עשו ופסילי ונסכי צום. To say: what is this about idolatry (ע\"ז) — 'and their idols and molten images he commanded them' — so too Jonadab commanded his sons not to serve idolatry (ע\"ז), and likewise Jacob, when he sought to reveal the End to his sons and it was hidden from him, said: perhaps there are among you idolaters (עובדי ע\"ז) — they said to him: Hear O Israel."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {0 "The third Masorah citation appears to quote Deuteronomy 4:28 (ופסילי ונסכי) rather than the form with צום found in Deuteronomy 29:16; rendered hyper-literally as the Hebrew stands. ע\"א in the phrase 'ע\"א מדבר' is unclear; possibly a variant or corruption for ע\"ז (idolatry), translated contextually."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:18:55.673335888Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}